        ("How does AWQ (Activation-aware Weight Quantization) preserve model accuracy at 4-bit precision better than standard round-to-nearest (RTN)?",
         "Standard round-to-nearest (RTN) quantization treats all weight channels equally, but empirical observation shows that in LLMs, less than 1% of weight channels (salient weights) account for the vast majority of output variance. When these critical weights are truncated to 4-bit integers, perplexity degrades severely.\n\nAWQ analyzes activation distributions during calibration. It identifies the salient channels and scales their weight values upward before quantization, while inversely scaling the corresponding activations. This protects the salient weights from quantization rounding error without altering the mathematical output, allowing 4-bit models to match full 16-bit FP16 accuracy.")
